---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="SCORE dataset" description="How to generate reproducible open-source SoC RTL snapshots with SCORE scripts.">
  <div class="page prose">
    <h1>SCORE dataset</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      SCORE (System-on-Chip Verilog RTL modules dataset for EDA research) pins upstream revisions and documents one install → generate → run path per architecture so EDA experiments share the same RTL artifacts.
    </p>

    <h2>Typical workflow</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Install</strong> — <code class="mono">scripts/install_&lt;arch&gt;.sh</code> prepares toolchains and dependencies.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Generate</strong> — <code class="mono">scripts/generate_&lt;arch&gt;.sh</code> exports RTL under
        <code class="mono">datasets/&lt;architecture&gt;/&lt;commit&gt;/</code> with logs beside the snapshot.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Run</strong> — where present, <code class="mono">scripts/run_&lt;arch&gt;.sh</code> replays smoke/simulation checks.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Coverage</h2>
    <p>
      Architectures wired through SCORE scripts are marked <span class="chip chip--ember">SCORE integrated</span> in the
      <a href={`${base}architectures/`}>catalog</a>. External registry entries (for example Chipyard, ESP, LiteX, Basilisk, BOOM) appear for survey completeness even when they are not yet in the generate harness.
    </p>

    <h2>Licensing</h2>
    <p>
      RTL snapshots and submodule trees follow each upstream project’s license. SCORE-authored scripts and docs are offered under
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Full details live in the repository
      <a href="https://github.com/SJTU-YONGFU-RESEARCH-GRP/score/blob/main/README.md">README.md</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
